{"step_index":1824,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:05Z","input_tokens":2073,"cache_read_tokens":36976,"output_tokens":1966,"thinking":"Initial setup involves instantiating `TeachMeCodeApp`, establishing a foundational object. Deciding between adding methods to `TeachMeCodeApp` or having `DsaDashboard` call `window.teachMeApp.loadProblem(problem)` shapes the architecture. The approach leans toward creating a focused, dedicated module: `app_build/dsa_dashboard.js`.\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nConsidering how to manage and persist user progress data, initially focusing on local storage for state management and defining the data schema for tracking solved, attempted, bookmarked problems along with user history and notes. Calculating and presenting real-time progress metrics is crucial, factoring in total problems, solved problems, and attempts to dynamically calculate a completion rate. This will integrate problem difficulty and topic breakdowns to provide a comprehensive progress dashboard.\n\n\nAnalyzing the data structure for the DSA topics, problem counts, solved counts, progress bars and filtering implementation is next. Implementing the \"Continue Learning\" card logic involves checking for a previous problem ID and displaying relevant details. Building the \"Recently Practiced Problems\" section requires fetching and displaying up to eight most recent sessions. Lastly, I will create the \"Beginner Learning Roadmap\" with its structured phases.\n\n\nAnalyzing the problem library structure, focusing on representing DSA phases with titles, descriptions, and problem counts. Each phase will include solved/total problem counts, milestone badges, and filtering functionality. The search, filter, and sort features require implementing a real-time search input field, topic and difficulty filters, status filters, and sorting options.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath"